2026-10-16T00:51:36.2066630Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2077539Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2183833Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2194292Z [0m
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2195354Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2196285Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2196691Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2196996Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2197546Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2197959Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2198326Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2199100Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2199468Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2200139Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2201150Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2202033Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2203139Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2203500Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2203860Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2204419Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2204835Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2205912Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2206214Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2206452Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2206786Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2207430Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2208391Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2209071Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2209322Z I will:
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2209594Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2209933Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2210681Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2211179Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2211654Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2211992Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2212318Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2212831Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2213274Z    /root
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2225536Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2226413Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2237169Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2238105Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2238887Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2241850Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2242461Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2258666Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2259418Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2269497Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2270221Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2271044Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2271476Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2271795Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2272255Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2272638Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2273489Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2273932Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2274164Z If you would like to
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2274879Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2275230Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2275439Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2276110Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2276314Z 
2026-10-16T00:51:36.2276318Z 
